Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 01:31:35 +0000

Not every replacement carries a Link line. A series may be replaced by
a different one, or posted again without naming the old version, and
it then stays current forever.

A maintainer can now retire such a thread by replying to it with a
Superseded-by trailer as the last lines of the reply. The trailer
names the replacement, so the link survives on the list, and the tag
is derived from it like every other.

Trailers are found with git interpret-trailers, so they follow the
same rules as in commit messages. A trailer quoted in a later reply
does not count, so quoting the old message does not retire anything
by accident.
