change-id: lmozpmvnnwylpvukyuozmwytyzssynzp

This is the manual half of superseded tracking. To retire a thread
that no "Link to vN" line names, reply to it and end the reply with

    Superseded-by: id:<message-id of the replacement>

as the last paragraph, or just above a signature. The whole thread
the reply sits in is tagged superseded on the next "notmuch new".
The value is not checked; it records where the work went.

It needs "[PATCH v3] notmuch: Tag series a later version replaces"
[1], which is not yet applied; its patch id is on the
prerequisite-patch-id line below.

I ran the hook from this commit against a copy of the notmuch
database, with four test replies added to untagged threads. A
closing trailer and one above a signature each tagged their thread;
a quoted trailer and one followed by more text did not. The 21
messages already on the list that mention "superseded by" tag
nothing new, so it tags the same 32 threads as the prerequisite
alone, and a second run tags the same set.

